/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.1 IPv4 Addressing Architecture and Classful Allocation) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(An Internet Protocol \(IP\) address is a 32-bit unique numerical identifier assigned to) Tj
T*
(every network interface card \(NIC\) connected to an IP network:) Tj
T*
(* Dotted-Decimal Notation: 32 bits divided into four 8-bit octets separated by) Tj
T*
(periods \(e.g., 192.168.1.1\). Range of each octet: 0 to 255.) Tj
T*
(* Original Classful Addressing Scheme \(RFC 791\):) Tj
T*
(- Class A: First bit 0 \(Range: 1.0.0.0 to 126.255.255.255\). 8 network bits, 24 host) Tj
T*
(bits. 126 networks, 16.7 million hosts each. Default mask: 255.0.0.0 \(/8\).) Tj
T*
(- Class B: First bits 10 \(Range: 128.0.0.0 to 191.255.255.255\). 16 network bits, 16 host) Tj
T*
(bits. 16,384 networks, 65,534 hosts each. Default mask: 255.255.0.0 \(/16\).) Tj
T*
(- Class C: First bits 110 \(Range: 192.0.0.0 to 223.255.255.255\). 24 network bits, 8 host) Tj
T*
(bits. 2 million networks, 254 hosts each. Default mask: 255.255.255.0 \(/24\).) Tj
T*
(- Class D: First bits 1110 \(Range: 224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255\). Reserved for Multicast) Tj
T*
(group addressing.) Tj
T*
(- Class E: First bits 1111 \(Range: 240.0.0.0 to 255.255.255.255\). Reserved for) Tj
T*
(experimental research.) Tj
T*
(* Loopback Address: 127.0.0.1 \(localhost\) used for internal software diagnostics.) Tj
T*
(* Private IP Ranges \(RFC 1918 - non-routable on public Internet\):) Tj
T*
(- Class A: 10.0.0.0 to 10.255.255.255 \(10.0.0.0/8\)) Tj
T*
(- Class B: 172.16.0.0 to 172.31.255.255 \(172.16.0.0/12\)) Tj
T*
(- Class C: 192.168.0.0 to 192.168.255.255 \(192.168.0.0/16\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.2 Subnetting, CIDR and Variable Length Subnet Masking \(VLSM\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Subnetting: Borrowing host bits to create smaller, manageable subnetworks to reduce) Tj
T*
(broadcast traffic and enhance routing security.) Tj
T*
(* Classless Inter-Domain Routing \(CIDR\): Suffix notation \(/N\) indicating number of) Tj
T*
(contiguous masked network bits.) Tj
T*
(* Formulae for Subnet Calculations:) Tj
T*
ET

