T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 3: TCP 3-Way Handshake Connection Sequence Analysis]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Trace the sequence numbers, acknowledgment numbers, and TCP control) Tj
T*
(flags during the establishment and termination of a reliable connection between Client C) Tj
T*
(and Web Server S.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step TCP Protocol Sequence:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Handshake Step 1 \(SYN from Client\):) Tj
T*
(- Client sends SYN packet to Server with an Initial Sequence Number \(ISN_c = 5000\).) Tj
T*
(Control flag: SYN = 1, ACK = 0.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Handshake Step 2 \(SYN-ACK from Server\):) Tj
T*
(- Server receives SYN, allocates buffer resources, and replies with SYN-ACK. Server) Tj
T*
(selects its own Initial Sequence Number \(ISN_s = 8000\). Acknowledgment Number = ISN_c +) Tj
T*
(1 = 5001. Control flags: SYN = 1, ACK = 1.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Handshake Step 3 \(ACK from Client\):) Tj
T*
(- Client replies with ACK packet. Sequence Number = 5001. Acknowledgment Number = ISN_s) Tj
T*
(+ 1 = 8001. Control flags: SYN = 0, ACK = 1.) Tj
T*
(- Connection state transitions to ESTABLISHED on both endpoints. Data transfer) Tj
T*
(commences.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Connection Teardown \(4-Way Handshake\):) Tj
T*
(- Client sends FIN \(FIN=1, ACK=1\). Server replies with ACK. \(Half-closed: server can) Tj
T*
(still send remaining data\).) Tj
T*
(- Server completes transmission and sends FIN. Client replies with final ACK and enters) Tj
T*
(TIME_WAIT state \(2 x MSL = 120 s\) to ensure ACK reaches server safely before closing) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
