([PROBLEM 4: Walkthrough of DHCP DORA and DNS Iterative Resolution]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Trace the exact sequence of network protocol packets when an) Tj
T*
(unconfigured laptop connects to an enterprise campus Wi-Fi network and requests webpage) Tj
T*
("www.lpu.in".) Tj
T*
(End-to-End Network Protocol Flow:) Tj
T*
(* 1. DHCP Discover: Laptop broadcasts UDP packet from 0.0.0.0:68 to) Tj
T*
(255.255.255.255:67 with its MAC address.) Tj
T*
(* 2. DHCP Offer: Campus DHCP server reserves IP 10.20.30.45 and offers it to client) Tj
T*
(along with subnet mask 255.255.255.0, default gateway 10.20.30.1, and DNS server) Tj
T*
(10.20.1.10.) Tj
T*
(* 3. DHCP Request: Laptop broadcasts formal request to lease offered IP 10.20.30.45.) Tj
T*
(* 4. DHCP ACK: Server confirms lease in binding database; laptop configures network) Tj
T*
(adapter.) Tj
T*
(* 5. ARP Resolution: Laptop checks if default gateway MAC is cached; sends ARP) Tj
T*
(request for 10.20.30.1 to obtain gateway MAC.) Tj
T*
(* 6. DNS Resolution: Laptop sends UDP query to DNS server \(10.20.1.10\) for) Tj
T*
("www.lpu.in".) Tj
T*
(* 7. Iterative DNS Query Hierarchy: Local DNS queries Root Server \(.\) -> TLD Server) Tj
T*
(\(.in\) -> Authoritative Nameserver \(lpu.in\) -> Returns IP 14.139.242.10 to laptop.) Tj
T*
(* 8. TCP Connection: Laptop initiates TCP 3-Way Handshake with 14.139.242.10 on port) Tj
T*
(443 \(HTTPS\).) Tj
T*
